("Amazon Connect and Teams", "t14", "A customer pattern uses an SBC between Teams Direct Routing and Amazon Connect or a SIP voice connector. It is a bridge you design, not a Microsoft Calling Plan feature.", "Confirm the current vendor docs before you promise agent whisper or recording.", "Draw the SIP path and the identifier you will store.", "Both platforms record and neither capture has the Call-ID.", "dr"),
("Call Automation", "t15", "The ACS server-side calling API. Your app answers, plays, recognizes DTMF or speech, and transfers. You receive events. You do not drive a desktop click.", "It is the IVR runtime, not the Teams client.", "Subscribe to the events and time out the recognize step.", "The app never answers, so the caller hears ringing until the platform gives up.", "acs"),
("Calling SDK", "t15", "The ACS client SDK for a human in a browser or a mobile app. Different from Call Automation, which is the server.", "Teams interop has its own requirements on top of either one.", "Pick the SDK if a person is on the page. Pick automation if a bot answers.", "A web page uses the calling SDK and nobody handles the server events.", "acs"),
("Recognize step", "t15", "The Call Automation action that collects DTMF or speech. It needs a timeout and a path for ‘none of the above.’", "A recognize step without an escape traps the caller.", "Map 0 to a human queue and test it.", "The bot repeats the prompt until the caller hangs up.", "acs"),
("Azure AI Speech", "t15", "Microsoft’s speech-to-text and text-to-speech service. Copilot Studio and custom IVRs can use it. It is not emergency calling.", "A custom neural voice has its own approval rules. Do not assume you can clone a person.", "Choose a voice you are allowed to use and log the recognition result.", "The prompt language does not match the caller and every intent is unknown.", "speech"),
("Copilot Studio voice agent", "t15", "A bot built in Copilot Studio that can front a voice channel, including Dynamics contact-center voice, using topics or generative orchestration.", "Generative answers still need an escape to a human and a knowledge source you trust.", "Publish the agent, attach it to the channel, and test the escape digit.", "The agent is the only target of the public number, including emergencies.", "copilot"),
("Azure AI Foundry", "t15", "The Azure portal family for models, agents, and evaluations. The earlier name was Azure AI Studio. It does not route PSTN.", "A model demo is not a contact-center design.", "Evaluate a prompt against a test set before you put it on a phone number.", "A model change ships to the IVR with no eval.", "foundry"),
("Teams interop with ACS", "t15", "ACS can be set up to call Teams users and to join Teams meetings when the interop prerequisites are met.", "A raw ACS number does not automatically become a Teams user.", "Follow the current interop article for the resource you created.", "The bot can call the PSTN and cannot transfer to a Teams expert.", "acs"),
("MS-700", "t16", "MS-700 is still live, with a skills update on Oct 27 2026; it is NOT retired and has no replacement. It is the exam for Microsoft 365 Certified: Teams Administrator Associate.", "Rumors that it was replaced by an MS-220 collaboration exam are not what Learn says.", "Study the current guide, including network and call-quality objectives. There is no replacement exam.", "A candidate skips networking because they think the exam is only meetings.", "ms700"),
("MB-280 retired", "t16", "MB-280 retired Jul 31 2026, with AB-210 as its successor; AB-210 is in beta. It covered Sales and Customer Insights, not the contact-center product.", "People still put it on a contact-center study plan.", "Do not book MB-280. AB-210 is its successor and is in beta. AB-250 is the contact-center exam.", "A job post requires MB-280 after the retirement date.", "retire"),
("AB-210", "t16", "Dynamics 365 Sales AI Consultant Associate. AB-210 is the successor to MB-280 and is in beta. It is not a replacement for MS-700.", "It is the wrong exam for a contact-center engineer.", "Use AB-250 when the job is Dynamics 365 Contact Center. Use AB-210 only for a sales role, and remember it is in beta.", "Study time goes to sales Copilot for a queue-routing role.", "partner"),
("AB-250", "t16", "Transforming Contact Center Experiences with AI in Dynamics 365. It earns Dynamics 365 Contact Center AI Engineer Associate. Pass mark is 700. The public page allows 120 minutes.", "The beta discount ran through 18 June 2026. Confirm the seat you can book now.", "Study deploy, channels, agents, work distribution, the representative experience, and analytics.", "A candidate revises MB-280 practice tests for this exam.", "ab250"),
("AZ-900", "t16", "Azure Fundamentals. It was not on the retirement list reviewed on 14 October 2026.", "Useful context for ACS and Speech. It will not teach you a dial plan.", "Take it if you need Azure vocabulary, not instead of MS-700.", "A voice design is approved because someone passed AZ-900.", "az900"),
("SC-900", "t16", "Security, Compliance, and Identity Fundamentals. The English certification is scheduled to update on 21 October 2026.", "It frames Entra ID and compliance. It does not configure an SBC.", "Read the current study guide after the 21 October update if you sit it later.", "Conditional Access is treated as out of scope for a voice project.", "sc900"),
("MS-900 retired", "t16", "Microsoft 365 Fundamentals retired on 31 March 2026.", "Do not recommend it as the starting exam.", "Use role exams and the product docs.", "A learning path still tells a new hire to book MS-900.", "retire"),
("AI-900 retired", "t16", "Azure AI Fundamentals retired on 30 June 2026.", "Speech and Copilot Studio are learned from their own docs now.", "Do not use a retired fundamentals exam as the AI plan.", "The study plan lists AI-900 beside AB-250.", "retire"),
("Passing score 700", "t16", "Microsoft role-based exams, including MS-700 and AB-250, require 700 out of 1000.", "A practice percentage is not the same scale unless the practice says so.", "Use the official practice assessment when one exists.", "Someone stops studying at a 70 percent practice score on a different scale.", "ms700"),
("Convenience recording", "t17", "A user starts a recording of a call, meeting, or event. Policy can allow it. The user can stop it. Storage follows meeting rules.", "It is not a compliance program. Guests cannot start it.", "Set the meeting, calling, and events policies on purpose.", "A regulated desk is told to ‘just hit record.’", "rec"),
("Compliance recording", "t17", "A third-party recorder is invited by policy into new calls, meetings, and events. The user does not start it and participant consent is not the control. Notification is enforced.", "The comparison table says audio-only is not the compliance mode. Media listed is voice, video, and screen share.", "Create the application instance, enable the policy, grant it, and test a new call.", "The policy is granted and nothing records because the bot instance was never created.", "rec"),
("Compliance recording application", "t17", "The bot instance of a certified recorder. The policy references it. Without it, granting the policy does not record.", "Work with the recorder vendor for the application ID. Do not invent one.", "New-CsTeamsComplianceRecordingApplication attaches it to the policy.", "Recording works in the vendor’s cloud and never joins the Teams call.", "recsetup"),
("Existing calls are unaffected", "t17", "When you grant a compliance recording policy, calls and meetings already up are not swept in. Test with a new call.", "A pilot that reuses an open meeting proves nothing.", "Place a fresh call after the grant and confirm the bot joined.", "The pilot says recording failed because they watched an old meeting.", "recps"),
("Quality management", "t17", "Listening to and scoring recorded interactions. Often the same vendor as compliance recording, sometimes a separate one.", "QM needs the recording first. A score without audio is a rumor.", "Define the form, the sample, and who may listen.", "Supervisors export recordings to a laptop share.", "rec"),
("Workforce management", "t17", "Scheduling and adherence for a queue. It eats interval stats, handle time, and shrinkage. It is not a feature of a Teams user policy.", "Teams Call Analytics will not staff next Tuesday.", "Feed offered, answered, abandoned, and handle time from the queue or the CCaaS.", "WFM says you were overstaffed while the queue overflowed, because overflow removed the calls from the count.", "d365"),
("Shrinkage", "t17", "The fraction of paid time that is not available for contacts: leave, training, meetings, breaks.", "Erlang C tells you how many people must be on the phone. Shrinkage tells you how many to roster.", "Publish the assumption. A 30 percent guess should be labeled as a guess.", "The schedule staffs the Erlang number and half the team is in training.", "d365"),
("Occupancy", "t17", "Handle time divided by handle time plus available time. High occupancy feels efficient and burns people out.", "WFM and quality fight here.", "Watch it beside service level, not instead of service level.", "A site celebrates 95 percent occupancy and abandonment climbs.", "d365"),
("Service level", "t17", "The fraction of contacts answered inside a target, for example 80 percent in 20 seconds. Erlang C is one teaching model of it.", "Averages hide the tail.", "Write the target, the interval, and the abandonment rule.", "Two vendors compute abandoned calls differently and both claim the target.", "d365"),
("Power BI and CQD", "t17", "Power BI can sit on top of Call Quality Dashboard data. It does not replace Call Analytics for one call, and it inherits a bad subnet map.", "A pretty report of the wrong building is still wrong.", "Fix the building and subnet dimensions before you publish a dashboard.", "Leadership sees a red HQ that is actually the VPN pool.", "cqd"),
("Screen pop", "t17", "The CRM opens the contact that matches the caller. Teams does not do this by itself for an ordinary PSTN call.", "The contact center or a middleware has to pass an E.164 number or a case id.", "Normalize before the lookup. Store the Call-ID on the timeline.", "The pop shows the wrong person because the trunk prefix was still on the number.", "d365"),
("E.164", "t06", "The international form of a number, starting with + and a country code. Routes and CRM lookups should use it after normalization.", "Raw digits mean different things in different countries.", "Normalize first, then route, then look up.", "The CRM stores 0207… and the SBC stores +44207… and they never join.", "dial"),
("Call-ID", "t17", "The SIP header that identifies one dialog. It is the join key between an SBC capture, a carrier ticket, and a CRM note.", "A timestamp is not an identifier. Two calls start in the same second.", "Write the Call-ID into the system you will have open during an incident.", "Support has a CRM case and an SBC log and cannot prove they are the same call.", "dr"),
("Integration seam", "t17", "A named place where another system is allowed to attach: a policy, a queue overflow, a subnet list, an event, an identifier.", "A seam you do not name becomes a rewrite.", "Document the seam in the same change as the feature.", "Recording is added a year later and the number plan has to change.", "cc"),
("Human escape", "t17", "A digit or intent that always reaches a person. Voice agents need one. Emergency numbers need a real route, not a bot.", "A bot that cannot fail open will trap callers.", "Test the escape on every prompt change.", "The prompt says ‘say agent’ and the recognize step has no such intent.", "copilot"),
("Certificate expiry seam", "t17", "The date the SBC certificate stops being valid. It is an integration hook because every carrier and every proxy will notice it on the same morning.", "Calendar it like a license, not like a surprise.", "Monitor the date and renew before the TLS handshake fails.", "OPTIONS fail on a Saturday and the dial plan is blamed.", "dr"),
("Subnet as a shared list", "t17", "The same subnet definitions should feed emergency location, location-based routing, and the CQD building report.", "Three spreadsheets drift.", "Give one team the edit right and publish the list.", "E911 says London, CQD says VPN, LBR says Manchester.", "emerg"),
("Queue interval", "t17", "A 15-minute or 30-minute bucket of offered, answered, and abandoned contacts. WFM and Erlang C both assume you know the bucket.", "Mixing daily totals into a 30-minute formula is a unit error.", "Export the same interval the schedule uses.", "The forecast is ten times too high because the interval was a day.", "d365"),
("Abandon", "t17", "A caller who hangs up before an agent answers. Whether short abandons count is a business rule.", "Two reports with different abandon rules cannot be compared.", "Write the rule down and use it in WFM and in the service-level report.", "Service level is met only because abandons under five seconds were deleted.", "d365"),
("Average handle time", "t17", "Talk time plus after-call work, unless your definition says otherwise. Erlang traffic is calls times handle time divided by the interval.", "A handle time that forgets after-call work understaffs the queue.", "Measure it from the contact center, not from a stopwatch on one call.", "The Erlang sheet uses talk time only and the agents never finish wrap-up.", "d365"),
("PIDF-LO", "t08", "A location object that can be carried in a SIP INVITE for an emergency call so the far end sees where the caller is.", "It does not replace a carrier who knows how to route emergency calls in that country.", "Confirm the SBC passes it and the carrier reads it.", "The location is stripped at the SBC and the PSAP gets the trunk’s address only.", "emerg"),
("On-site notification", "t08", "An emergency calling policy can notify people on site when an emergency call is placed.", "Security who are not notified will meet the responders in the wrong lobby.", "Test the notification with the carrier’s test process, not with a real emergency call.", "The test notifies nobody because the policy was never assigned.", "emerg"),
("GCC High SIP", "t05", "Office 365 GCC High uses sip.pstnhub.gov.teams.microsoft.us. Do not copy the commercial three-proxy list into a government tenant.", "The commercial names will not be the signaling peers.", "Read the plan page for the cloud you are actually in.", "A commercial runbook is pasted into GCC High.", "dr"),
("DoD SIP", "t05", "Office 365 DoD uses sip.pstnhub.dod.teams.microsoft.us.", "Same failure as using commercial names in the wrong cloud.", "Use the DoD name from the current plan page.", "The SBC peers with sip.pstnhub.microsoft.com from a DoD tenant.", "dr"),
("IPv6 SIP proxies", "t05", "The plan page also lists sip.ipv6.pstnhub.microsoft.com and the sip2 and sip3 IPv6 names, resolving into 2603:1063:400::/40.", "An IPv6-only SBC that was given the IPv4 names never peers.", "Match the address family you actually route.", "Firewall objects exist only for IPv4.", "dr"),
("Early offer", "t10", "Teams Direct Routing presents media in the INVITE. An SBC or CUBE that waits for a delayed offer will negotiate badly.", "488 and one-way audio show up when the offer model is wrong.", "Set the vendor profile for early offer toward Teams.", "CUCM sends delayed offer all the way to Teams.", "cube"),
("AudioCodes", "t10", "A certified SBC family. Mediant devices and their management tools are common in Direct Routing designs. The Microsoft certified list is the support boundary, the vendor guide is the config.", "Naming the brand is not a design.", "Follow AudioCodes’ current Teams document for the firmware you run.", "A forum config from 2019 is pasted onto new firmware.", "audiocodes"),
("Ribbon SBC", "t10", "Ribbon’s certified session border controllers are a Direct Routing option. Core and software editions differ.", "The support path is Ribbon first, then Microsoft if the vendor escalates.", "Use Ribbon’s current Teams guide and a public certificate.", "OPTIONS are answered on the wrong interface.", "ribbon"),
("Oracle SBC", "t10", "Oracle Communications Session Border Controller can be certified for Direct Routing on specific releases. Check the Microsoft list for the release, not the logo.", "An unlisted release is an unsupported trunk.", "Match the certified software version and the certificate name.", "The beautiful config is one release below the certified list.", "oracle"),
("Cisco CUBE", "t10", "Cisco Unified Border Element on IOS-XE, when the release is certified, is a normal Direct Routing SBC and the usual bridge to CUCM.", "CUBE is still an SBC. It does not make Teams ‘speak SCCP.’", "Use Cisco’s current CUBE for Teams guide. Trust the signaling ranges. Present the paired name.", "A voice engineer applies a SIP trunk to CUCM and never peers with the pstnhub names.", "cube"),
("Vendor-first support", "t10", "Microsoft’s Direct Routing support boundary: you call the SBC vendor, they escalate to Microsoft if they must. Non-certified SBCs can be refused.", "Opening a Microsoft case with a homemade SBC wastes the outage.", "Keep the certified-list screenshot with the firmware version.", "A ticket is opened with no SBC logs and no firmware.", "sbcs"),
("Analog via Direct Routing", "t09", "Fax, door phones, and elevators usually stay on an SBC or SIP Gateway, not on a Teams client.", "A Calling Plan user license does not give you an elevator phone.", "Put analog on the SBC design and test the emergency path from that device.", "The elevator is moved to Teams as a user and cannot dial during a WAN cut.", "sipgw"),
("Presence-based routing", "t07", "A queue can skip agents whose Teams presence says they are busy or in a meeting.", "An agent who never sets presence will take every serial call or none, depending on the rest of the design.", "Decide the presence rule and test with one agent in a meeting.", "Agents set themselves to Do Not Disturb to leave the queue, and nobody notices for a week.", "cq"),
("Opt out of a queue", "t07", "Agents can be allowed to leave a queue. If you forbid it, staffing math must include breaks or they will dodge in other ways.", "WFM adherence and the queue opt-out flag are the same argument.", "Pick one policy and tell the supervisors.", "The schedule says five agents and three have opted out.", "cq"),
("Callback", "t07", "A queue feature that calls the customer back. The prerequisite article treats callback as a case that needs funding on the resource account.", "Callback is an outbound PSTN call, not a setting with no carrier.", "Fund pay-as-you-go or credits, then test one callback.", "The option is on and every callback fails.", "prereq"),
("Graph communications", "t14", "Microsoft Graph APIs used by Extend and by recording and presence integrations. They are not a SIP trunk.", "A design that says ‘we will use Graph instead of an SBC’ still needs a PSTN path.", "Use Graph for the app, and Calling Plans, Operator Connect, or Direct Routing for the telephone network.", "Presence is synced and audio is not connected.", "cc"),
("Policy recording bot join", "t17", "The recorder joins as an application because the user’s policy names it. If the bot fails to join, you have a policy, an ID, or a media problem, in that order.", "Do not start with the carrier.", "Check Enabled, the application instance, and the grant, then the vendor’s join log.", "The carrier is asked for a recording they never made.", "recsetup"),
("Retention of recordings", "t17", "Compliance recordings are retained by the partner’s system, not by Teams meeting storage. Convenience recordings follow meeting storage.", "Legal hold on a mailbox does not automatically hold the partner’s audio.", "Write the retention in the partner contract and test a restore.", "A regulator asks for a call and the partner’s bucket expired.", "rec"),
("Evaluation form", "t17", "The QM scorecard. It should cite behaviors you can hear, not vibes.", "A form that scores ‘professionalism’ without a definition will not survive an argument.", "Publish the form before you score people.", "Agents are coached on a form they have never seen.", "rec"),
("Screen recording", "t17", "Often a QM vendor feature on the agent desktop. Teams compliance recording’s documented media list is voice, video, and screen share inside the Teams session, which is not the same as a silent desktop recorder.", "Do not claim Teams records the CRM screen unless the product you bought does.", "If you need the desktop, buy and disclose that recorder.", "A privacy review finds a desktop recorder nobody mentioned.", "rec"),
("Building map", "t17", "The table that says which subnet is which building in CQD. It is only as good as the subnets you typed.", "A wrong building makes a dashboard accuse the wrong LAN.", "Reconcile it with the emergency subnet list.", "Facilities rebuilds a floor and both maps stay old.", "cqd"),
("Admin roles for CQD", "t12", "CQD is an admin report, not a personal call history. The people who can open it are the roles you grant, not every user.", "A manager with no role will ask for a screenshot instead of access.", "Grant the smallest role that can see the report.", "CQD credentials are shared.", "cqd"),
("After-call work", "t17", "Time the agent spends in the CRM after the caller hangs up. Include it in handle time if your WFM definition says so.", "Leaving it out makes Erlang C look generous.", "Define it and measure it from the contact-center state, not from memory.", "Agents are ‘available’ in Teams while still writing the case.", "d365"),
("Skill-based routing", "t13", "Assignment that prefers a representative who has the skill the classification step wrote on the work item.", "Skills that exist on a slide and not on the user do nothing.", "Attach skills to people and to the classification rules, then test a miss.", "Every item requires a skill nobody has, so the queue never assigns.", "ab250"),
("Intent-based routing", "t13", "Classification that uses an intent, often from a bot or a model, to pick a queue.", "An intent of ‘unknown’ needs a default queue.", "Map unknown to a human, not to a retry loop.", "The model returns unknown and the caller is played the same prompt.", "ab250"),
("Proactive outbound", "t13", "Contact-center campaigns that place calls outward. They need a number, a consent story, and a capacity plan.", "They are not a Teams user’s personal redial.", "Follow the current channel article for outbound, and fund the numbers.", "A campaign uses a user’s caller ID and the CRM trust collapses.", "ab250"),
("Real-time translation", "t13", "A channel feature that can translate a conversation. It is not a substitute for a language queue when the policy says a human must speak the language.", "Translation errors in a regulated script are your errors.", "Decide where translation is allowed and where a skilled human is required.", "A billing dispute is translated badly and the case notes disagree.", "ab250"),
("Knowledge source", "t15", "The documents a Copilot or a generative agent is allowed to quote. If the source is wrong, the answer is wrong with confidence.", "Ground the agent or do not put it on the phone.", "Limit the sources and test questions whose answers you already know.", "The agent quotes a retired price list.", "copilot"),
("Generative orchestration", "t15", "The Copilot Studio mode that chooses topics and tools from the conversation, as opposed to a rigid topic tree.", "It needs tighter safety because the path is not a single menu.", "Keep the human escape outside the model’s mood.", "The agent talks a caller out of the escape phrase.", "copilot"),
("Classic topics", "t15", "The menu-like Copilot Studio design. Predictable and easier to test. Weaker on paraphrase.", "Use it when the call must follow a script.", "Write the topics, the entities, and the fallback.", "Fallback is empty and the caller hears silence.", "copilot"),
("Event Grid", "t15", "One way ACS delivers call events to your app. If the subscription is wrong, your IVR never sees RecognizeCompleted.", "The call can be up and your code asleep.", "Log the event type and the call id.", "The app polls a database and the events expired.", "acs"),
("DTMF relay", "t11", "Digits in the audio path or as telephone-events. IVRs fail when the SBC strips them.", "A human can talk and the bot never hears 1.", "Test digits through every SBC, not only Teams-to-Teams.", "The queue escape works in the lab and fails through the carrier.", "dr"),
("Comfort noise and SID", "t04", "Silence suppression changes the average bitrate. Do not size a link only from a G.711 average that assumed comfort noise you did not enable.", "The peak is still the number that fills the queue.", "Size for the codec you offer, per direction, at the packetization you set.", "The link was sized for silence and the all-hands call filled it.", "qos"),
("Packetization 20 ms", "t04", "The usual voice packet interval in these bandwidth figures. A 10 ms interval doubles the header tax.", "Changing ptime on the SBC changes the bandwidth you planned.", "Lock ptime in the design.", "One SBC uses 10 ms and the policer drops packets.", "qos"),
("Jitter buffer", "t12", "The client waits a little so late packets can still be played. Too small and you hear gaps. Too large and you talk over each other.", "CQD jitter and the buffer are related and not the same number.", "Fix the network before you hunt a hidden buffer setting.", "A WAN with 40 ms jitter is ‘fixed’ by a slide that says buffer.", "cqd"),
("Round-trip time", "t12", "How long a packet takes to go and come back. Long RTT with low loss means distance or hairpin, not a dirty cable.", "People add bandwidth and the delay stays.", "Look at the path. Bypass or local egress may beat a fatter pipe.", "A branch backhauls media across a continent.", "cqd"),
("DSCP rewrite", "t04", "A router or VPN that sets the mark back to 0. The client did its job and the path undid it.", "Verify at the egress, not only on the PC.", "Capture outside the VPN.", "The laptop shows EF and the WAN sees 0.", "qos"),
("Browser join ports", "t04", "People who join meetings in a browser do not use the fixed 50000-range client ports. An ACL that only matches those ports misses them.", "QoS designs that ignore browsers miss a real population.", "Say so in the design if many people join from browsers.", "Guests sound worse and the ACL is declared complete.", "qos"),
("Mac and mobile DSCP", "t04", "Mac, iOS, and Android use hard-coded audio EF and a hard-coded video and sharing mark. They are not the Windows policy object.", "A Windows-only QoS rollout looks done and is not.", "Still enable QoS in the admin center, and mark at the network for devices that will not cooperate.", "Mobile executives are the poor-quality population.", "qos"),
("ms-teams.exe", "t04", "The current Teams client process name used when you bind a Windows QoS policy. An old policy aimed at the classic client marks nothing.", "Policy that matches the wrong executable is a silent miss.", "Update the policy object and verify with a capture.", "QoS policy still names the previous client.", "qos"),
("Busy hour", "t17", "The hour you actually size. Average day divided by eight is not a busy hour.", "Erlang inputs are busy-interval numbers.", "Take the busy interval from the contact center, not from a yearly average.", "The link is fine at 11:00 and dead at 09:15.", "d365"),
("Dual running", "t14", "Both PBX and Teams carry live numbers during a move. Rollback needs the old route left intact.", "A cut with no rollback is a career event.", "Move a range, keep the old path, and write the backout.", "The old trunk is deleted on Friday.", "cube"),
("Number porting", "t05", "Moving a public number from one carrier to another. It has a date and a letter of authority. It is not a PowerShell metaphor.", "Direct Routing can use numbers the carrier already holds, so a port might be unnecessary.", "Confirm who owns the number before you promise a weekend cut.", "Two carriers route the same number on Monday.", "pstn"),
("Caller ID policy", "t06", "What outbound calls present. Resource-account outbound and user outbound are different policies.", "A queue that presents a user’s mobile number breaks trust.", "Set the calling identity on the voice app on purpose.", "Customers return a call and reach an employee’s personal desk.", "route"),
("Music on hold", "t07", "The audio a queue plays while a caller waits. Licensing and the file both matter, and silence is a choice you should make on purpose.", "Callers who hear nothing hang up, and abandon looks like a staffing crisis.", "Upload a file you have rights to, and test the timeout.", "A licensed song is uploaded.", "cq"),
("Voicemail overflow", "t07", "A respectable overflow target when nobody is left to answer. It depends on Cloud Voicemail and a mailbox for the account that owns it.", "Overflow to voicemail without a mailbox is a dead end.", "Test the overflow, then check that the message arrived.", "Callers are offered voicemail and the message is never deposited.", "vm"),
("Pilot number", "t07", "The public number on the first voice app. Everything else can be an internal target.", "People buy a number per menu option and then cannot afford to change the menu.", "One number, many targets, overflow included.", "Each menu option is a ported number and the carrier lead time runs the project.", "aa"),
("Security group policy assign", "t17", "Compliance recording and many Teams policies can be assigned to a group. A user in the wrong group is recorded, or not, as a consequence.", "Group sprawl is a voice defect.", "Use a group you can explain, and read the effective policy.", "A contractor group inherits recording and a privacy review fails.", "recsetup"),
("Effective policy", "t03", "The policy the user actually has after direct assignment and group assignment are resolved. The one you edited may not be it.", "Get-CsOnlineUser beats the portal memory.", "Read the effective value before and after the change.", "You update a policy that is not assigned.", "roles"),
("Lab tenant", "t03", "A tenant that is not production. Pair a lab SBC there. Do not discover certificate behavior on the company trunk.", "Production is where rollback costs money.", "Keep lab domains and lab certificates obvious.", "A lab FQDN is the production FQDN.", "dr"),
("Get-Help before Set", "t03", "Cmdlet parameters move between MicrosoftTeams module versions. Read help in the version you are about to run.", "A blog’s parameter list is not a contract.", "Get-Help cmdlet -Parameter * in the lab.", "A script from last year removes a number.", "dr"),
("Least privilege", "t01", "Use the telephony or communications role that can do the task. Global Administrator is not a voice habit.", "A shared global account makes every later audit useless.", "Named admin accounts, voice roles, and Conditional Access for admins.", "The SBC password and the global admin password are the same sticky note.", "roles"),
("Service number", "t05", "A number assigned to a resource account or conferencing, as opposed to a user’s personal number. The inventory and the license follow the connectivity option.", "A user number on a queue is how you lose the queue when the human leaves.", "Take service numbers from the carrier or Calling Plan inventory you actually have.", "The receptionist leaves and the main number leaves with them.", "phone"),
("Unassigned number treatment", "t06", "What Teams does with a number you own that is not assigned. Routing it to an attendant is a product choice you should make.", "Silence on a published-but-unassigned number looks like an outage.", "Point unknown numbers at an attendant or a message.", "A ported block has fifty silent numbers.", "route"),
("SIP options timer teaching model", "t11", "This campus treats repeated missed OPTIONS as a reason to pull a trunk. It does not publish Microsoft’s internal counter as if it were a documented integer.", "A lab timer is not a contractual timer.", "Watch the admin-center SBC status and the SBC’s own OPTIONS log together.", "Someone sets a script to fail over after one missed packet and flaps the trunk.", "dr"),
("Failover rehearsal", "t11", "Pull the primary proxy or the primary SBC in a window and prove the next one takes calls.", "A second gateway that has never received a call is a drawing.", "Rehearse, then put the result in the runbook.", "The outage is the first test.", "dr"),
("Codec intersection empty", "t11", "If the SBC and Teams offer no codec in common, the call fails, often with 488.", "Adding AMR-WB on a bypass trunk does not fix a G.711 refusal.", "Offer G.711 at minimum unless you have a measured reason not to.", "The SBC allows only G.729 and the far end does not.", "dr"),
("G.711 law", "t11", "A-law and μ-law are both G.711. A trunk that offers the wrong one still often interoperates, and sometimes does not. Offer both if the carrier is vague.", "This is a one-line SBC change, after you have a capture.", "Capture SDP and compare.", "A new country is added and audio sounds like noise.", "dr"),
("Comfort message", "t07", "The words the queue plays about position or wait. A lie (‘your call is important’) is still a design choice you can decline.", "Bad messages increase abandon.", "Say something true: whether you record, and whether you call back.", "The message promises a callback the queue cannot place.", "cq"),
("Recording disclosure", "t17", "Both convenience and compliance recording require participant notification. Compliance does not ask the participant for consent in the comparison Microsoft publishes.", "A silent compliance recorder is a legal problem, not a clever config.", "Confirm the partner’s announcement and test it.", "Notification is off because it ‘hurt the experience.’", "rec"),
("Do not record emergency", "t17", "Know whether your recorder and your policy include emergency calls, and follow the rule you were given. Do not route emergency calls into a bot so they can be ‘handled.’", "Emergency is a route, a location, and a carrier.", "Keep the emergency voice route boring and local.", "999 matches the IVR workstream.", "emerg"),
("CRM timeline", "t17", "The case note should carry the Call-ID, the number in E.164, the queue, and the agent. Then a later complaint can be found.", "A note that says ‘called customer’ cannot be audited.", "Make the screen pop write those fields.", "The case exists and the recording cannot be found.", "d365"),
("Future hook", "t17", "A seam left on purpose for a system you might add later, using a product that already exists. It is not a promise that Microsoft will ship a feature.", "Invented roadmap items fail audits.", "Name the hook, the identifier, and the failure if you skip it.", "A design depends on an unannounced SBC feature.", "cc"),
("Power model wording", "t14", "Older conversation says Power for the third contact-center model. The Learn article maintained on 14 October 2026 says Unify, Extend, and Connect.", "Using the old word without a mapping hides the media path.", "Ask the vendor which of the three current models they hold.", "The contract says Power and the network team opens no ports.", "cc"),
("Certified list changes", "t10", "The list of SBCs and contact-center solutions changes. A campus page is not the list.", "Quote the list the week you buy.", "Link the design to the current Microsoft page and the firmware.", "A purchase order cites a 2022 PDF.", "sbcs"),
("User transfer license", "t14", "In the Connect model, Microsoft’s documentation says the contact-center side does not need a phone-system license, and the Teams user who receives a transferred call does need Teams Phone and a number.", "Experts who ‘just answer in Teams’ still need a telephone.", "License the humans who receive transfers.", "The agent transfers and the expert’s client will not take the PSTN call.", "cc"),
("Trial is not a design", "t13", "A Dynamics or Teams trial proves a click path. It does not prove emergency calling, recording retention, or a busy hour.", "Pilots skip the boring gates.", "Write the gates: 911, recording, overflow, certificate, rollback.", "The pilot is declared production on Friday.", "d365"),
("Rollback", "t14", "The numbers go back to the old route if the new path fails. If you deleted the old route, you do not have a rollback.", "Dual-running exists so rollback is a script, not a rebuild.", "Keep the old trunk until the new path has a quiet week.", "The maintenance window ends with no public numbers.", "cube"),
("Evidence pack", "t12", "Call-ID, the policy you read, the ladder, and the CQD or Call Analytics row. One pack per hypothesis.", "Verbal ‘it failed’ is not a pack.", "Store the pack with the change ticket.", "The same outage is debugged from scratch next month.", "calla"),
("Contoso sample", "t01", "A fictional tenant name used in Microsoft samples and in this campus. It is not a customer.", "Examples use 555 numbers and example domains so nothing here is someone’s directory.", "Keep lab names obviously fake.", "A lab script is aimed at a real tenant by find-and-replace.", "dr"),
("Exam sandbox", "t16", "Microsoft’s practice UI for what an exam looks like. It is not the product lab.", "Use it so the tool is not a surprise. Still study the skills.", "Open the sandbox once before the appointment.", "The first time someone sees a lab item is during the exam.", "ms700"),
("Renewal assessment", "t16", "Role-based certifications expire unless you pass the free renewal on Learn. Retirement is a different event from expiry.", "A certification you earned and did not renew is not a retirement of the exam.", "Calendar the renewal. Re-read what changed.", "MS-700 lapses and the holder thinks the exam was retired.", "ms700c"),
("Study guide wins", "t16", "When this campus and a study guide disagree, the study guide accessed the week you sit the exam wins.", "Skills move. The 27 October 2026 MS-700 update is an example.", "Re-open the guide before you book.", "A candidate memorizes a third-party brain dump.", "ms700"),
